                                    <h1>Point of Sale (POS) Software Development: Retail &amp; F&amp;B Guide 2026</h1>
                                    <p>POS software has moved from cash-till replacement to the central nervous system of retail and F&B operations. A modern POS is inventory + payments + CRM + loyalty + kitchen ops + delivery — all with rigorous offline-first design because Wi-Fi is never reliable and business can't stop. Here is what a POS build actually looks like.</p>
                                    <h2>The 3 POS Categories</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Retail POS:</strong> SKU-heavy, barcode + variant management, inventory sync across channels, loyalty. Lightspeed, Vend, Shopify POS pattern.<br><strong>F&B POS:</strong> KDS integration, split bills, table map, delivery integration, kitchen printer control. Toast, Square F&B, Petpooja, POSist pattern.<br><strong>Service POS:</strong> Appointment-based, staff commission tracking, service packages. Fresha, Booksy, Zenoti pattern.</p>
                                    <h2>Offline-First Is Not Optional</h2>
                                    <p>POS must work fully offline for at least 8-24 hours. Sales continue, receipts print, inventory decrements locally, and everything syncs when the connection returns. Getting this right adds 30-40% to build cost but is table-stakes.</p>
                                    <h2>Hardware Integrations</h2>
                                    <p>Barcode scanners (Symbol, Honeywell, Datalogic), thermal receipt printers (Star, Epson, Zebra), kitchen printers, cash drawers, weight scales (grocery, deli), card readers (Square, mPOS, Pine Labs, Ingenico), fiscal printers where required (Italy, Portugal, GCC in some cases).</p>
                                    <h2>Tax + Compliance by Region</h2>
                                    <p><strong>India:</strong> GST invoice generation with HSN codes, e-invoicing above ₹5 Cr turnover, state-level entry / octroi (rare now).<br><strong>UAE:</strong> VAT-compliant tax invoice, ESR reporting, FTA e-invoicing coming.<br><strong>USA:</strong> Sales tax by state + local jurisdiction (Avalara / TaxJar integration). Some states require tax-exempt purchase workflows.<br><strong>UK:</strong> VAT-compliant, MTD (Making Tax Digital) reporting.<br><strong>Australia:</strong> GST-compliant, invoice requirements.</p>
                                    <h2>Cost + Timeline</h2>
                                    <p><strong>MVP (14-20 weeks):</strong> ₹22-50 lakh / $27K-60K. Basic POS + payments + inventory sync.<br><strong>Growth (22-32 weeks):</strong> ₹60 lakh - 1.5 Cr / $72K-180K. Multi-store, loyalty, advanced reporting, mobile.<br><strong>Enterprise (32-48 weeks):</strong> ₹1.5-4 Cr / $180K-480K. Full ERP integration, franchise / chain features, complex tax.</p>

                                    <div style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1a2e 0%, #16213e 100%); padding: 40px; border-radius: 12px; margin: 40px 0; text-align: center; color: #fff;">
